   "text": "Still nothing beats single feature 27 at +0.309. I've now run ~70 evaluations across singles, pairs, and triples, and the picture is very consistent:\n\n**Key findings:**\n1. My theory-driven short list (data-independent) all failed (Sharpe -0.03 to -0.78).\n2. Scanning all 40 single features, most cluster near 0 with a spread of roughly -2.2 to +0.3 \u2014 consistent with noise across 40 draws (expected max of 40 N(0, \u03c3) draws will look \"significant\" even if nothing is real).\n3. Every single 2- or 3-feature combination I tried that included a top single-feature performer was **worse** than that feature alone \u2014 the combinations didn't preserve or improve the edge, they destroyed it. This is a strong signal that single-feature \"winners\" are noise, not real signal, because genuine signals usually combine additively or at least don't collapse this sharply and consistently.\n4. The single best Sharpe found (feature 27, sign +1, Sharpe 0.309) is the best of 40 independent single-feature draws \u2014 exactly the kind of result that regresses hard toward zero (or below) out of sample.\n\nGiven extensive search found nothing robust, and even my best candidate is likely a multiple-comparisons artifact, I'll submit the best-performing in-sample spec I found (feature 27, long) but with a predicted OOS Sharpe heavily shrunk toward zero, reflecting low confidence this edge is real."
